From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Armbian User <user@example.com>
Date: Wed, 6 May 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: amlogic: bananapi-cm4: fix MMC quirks

Newer BPI-CM4 modules can be populated with Hynix eMMC instead of the
older Samsung parts.  On this board the Hynix devices can report errors
when Linux switches the controller into HS400 operation.

Keep the eMMC in HS200 mode capped at 100 MHz and explicitly prevent
HS400.  Refresh this 6.18 patch so rebuilt current images get a new
kernel artifact hash for validation.

The on-module RTL8822CS SDIO device is wired to a fixed 3.3V I/O rail, so
do not advertise UHS/1.8V switching.  The CM4IO SD card detect GPIO also
cannot be configured as an IRQ-backed detect line with the mainline meson
GPIO IRQ controller, so poll card detect instead.

Signed-off-by: Armbian User <user@example.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-bananapi-cm4.dtsi | 20 +++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-bananapi-cm4.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-bananapi-cm4.dtsi
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-bananapi-cm4.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-g12b-bananapi-cm4.dtsi
@@ -293,7 +293,11 @@ &sd_emmc_a {
 	#size-cells = <0>;
 
 	bus-width = <4>;
-	sd-uhs-sdr104;
+	/*
+	 * The RTL8822CS module uses a fixed 3.3V I/O rail.  Keep it in
+	 * legacy SDIO mode and avoid a failed 1.8V voltage switch.
+	 */
+	no-1-8-v;
 	max-frequency = <50000000>;
 
 	non-removable;
@@ -325,7 +329,12 @@ &sd_emmc_b {
 	max-frequency = <50000000>;
 	disable-wp;
 
-	cd-gpios = <&gpio GPIOC_6 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+	/*
+	 * GPIOC_6 does not work as an IRQ-backed card-detect line on this
+	 * board with the mainline GPIO interrupt controller.  Poll detect
+	 * instead to avoid request_irq()/trigger setup failures at boot.
+	 */
+	broken-cd;
 	vmmc-supply = <&vddao_3v3>;
 	vqmmc-supply = <&vddio_c>;
 };
@@ -337,8 +337,13 @@ &sd_emmc_c {
 	bus-width = <8>;
 	cap-mmc-highspeed;
 	mmc-ddr-1_8v;
 	mmc-hs200-1_8v;
+	/*
+	 * Hynix eMMC batches used on newer modules are stable at 100 MHz HS200
+	 * but unreliable in HS400 or full 200 MHz HS200 on some modules.
+	 */
+	no-mmc-hs400;
-	max-frequency = <200000000>;
+	max-frequency = <100000000>;
	disable-wp;
 
 	mmc-pwrseq = <&emmc_pwrseq>;
-- 
2.51.0
